evice created your recovery seed phrase, it wasn=E2=80=99t using strong eno=
ugh randomness of the =E2=80=9Csecret words,=E2=80=9D which were weaker and=
 more guessable than they should have been.</p><p style=3D"margin:10px 0">A=
ttackers figured this out using AI (allegedly) and yesterday quickly draine=
d hundreds of wallets. Rem as AI gets better expect more and more of this t=
o happen. </p><p style=3D"margin:10px 0">Estimates range from $38 million (=
=E2=89=88594 BTC from 500 wallets) up to as high as ~$70 million depending =
on the count. Most of the theft happened in less than an hour.</p><p style=
=3D"margin:10px 0">Coinkite (the maker) released emergency fixed firmware t=
he same day:</p><p style=3D"margin:10px 0">Mk3 =E2=86=92 version 4.2.0 or h=
igher</p><p style=3D"margin:10px 0">Mk4 / Mk5 =E2=86=92 5.6.0 or higher</p>=
<p style=3D"margin:10px 0">Q =E2=86=92 1.5.0Q or higher</p><h2>IMPORTANT PA=
RT </h2><blockquote><p style=3D"margin:10px 0">Just updating the firmware d=
oes not fix an already-created weak seed. You have to generate a brand-new =
seed on the fixed firmware and move your coins to the new wallet.</p></bloc=
kquote><p style=3D"margin:10px 0">This is why sentiment around self-custody=
 and cold wallets took a big hit =E2=80=94 people are scared that even =E2=
=80=9Cair-gapped=E2=80=9D hardware can still have hidden flaws. </p><p styl=
e=3D"margin:10px 0">I never had such a wallet but as you know I was always =
very fearful of self custody going way back to 2020 once value of BTC start=
ed to really increase. </p><p></p></div></td></tr>
